# Quality Gate Optimization
RULE: Quality gates must complete in <3 minutes. Use pytest-xdist, skip slow tests in quick mode, synthetic fixtures.
WHY: Fast feedback is essential; parallel agents must not overload.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md § Two-Pass Workflow Model

Two-pass model for agents:
- Pass 1: `bash scripts/quality-gates.sh` — full run (lint, tests, typecheck, codex, security)
- Pass 2: `bash scripts/quickmerge.sh "msg" --agent` — lightweight verify only (no tests, no act)

Flag semantics:
- `--agent` (agent/CI): skip act + skip tests — quickmerge is a fast format/lint/typecheck gate
- `--quick` (human): skip act only — tests still run
- `--agent --skip-typecheck`: lint + format + codex only

DO: Use pytest-xdist; mark slow tests; `--tb=short`; `--agent` for agent quickmerge; Pass 1 full QG before Pass 2 quickmerge
NEVER: Run slow tests in quick mode; skip parallel execution; exceed 5min total; use `--quick` from agent sessions
